      "id": "hf.s1777-yolov8n",
      "comment": "Object detector (YOLOv8n raw output; the graph bakes the decode, the converter recognizes the anchor-free head and wraps it with Core ML NMS). This export carries no metadata_props, so labels fall back to generic class_<i> and the probe asserts the class INDEX (not a label name). The confidence threshold sits far below the single survivor, and NMS collapses the mutually-overlapping near-full-image noise boxes, so the box count is stable under float drift. Expectations are onnxruntime's output0 decoded and cross-class-suppressed by scripts/generate_onnx_detection_oracle.py.",
      "fileName": "yolov8n-s1777.onnx",
